<Base title="StrapSheets privacy" description="What StrapSheets stores on the phone and what AdMob and RevenueCat receive.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>StrapSheets has no accounts. Job numbers, measurements, thread names you add, and the PDFs stay on the phone. Uninstalling the app deletes them. There is no server copy to erase.</p>
  <p>Email is sent by the mail app you already use. StrapSheets does not receive that message.</p>
  <h2>Ads</h2>
  <p>The free app shows one banner on the session list, and only when the phone has a connection. Google AdMob supplies it. AdMob can receive device identifiers and advertising data, including an advertising identifier. Before the first ad, the app shows Google's consent form. On iPhone it also asks for tracking permission. Pro hides the banner. Ads may be scarce until the live store listing is linked to AdMob.</p>
  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>RevenueCat records an anonymous id and the purchase history needed to know whether Pro is active. It is not tied to a name you type into StrapSheets. Apple or Google processes the payment.</p>
  <h2>Camera</h2>
  <p>A later measuring tool uses the camera to estimate a length. The picture is not saved. That tool is not part of the first release's measurements.</p>
  <p>The publisher is an individual. The legal name is the seller name on the App Store, and the address Google requires for subscriptions is on the Play listing. Write to <a href="mailto:support@strapsheets.agent-swarm.net">support@strapsheets.agent-swarm.net</a>.</p>
</Base>
